### Room background of the steel study, natural decays, one job (2026-11-20: can a TOF-trigger ON/OFF subtraction show
### U, Th and K at 50 ppm in steel, with the room's background included? condor/room_background_submit.sh writes and
### submits the jobs, bands floor and radon). The setup of macro/beam_steel_lyso.mac, as the beam run had it: the
### 20 x 20 x 1 cm plate at 32.5-33.5 cm on the pixel panel bmPanel (macro/panel_<bmPanel>.mac, centre at bmPanelZ cm)
### inside TOFmeter's default setup (10 cm lead roof and four 10 cm lead walls, open at the bottom; TOF stations, Al
### plates, steel frame), plus what the beam run did not have: a 30 cm concrete floor (block Floor, G4_CONCRETE,
### 2.3 g/cm3) under the whole world at -30..0 cm, on which the setup stands.
### Each event is one nucleus bmIonZ, bmIonA at rest, placed uniformly in the box rmX rmY rmZ +- rmHalfX rmHalfY rmHalfZ
### (cm) inside the volume rmVolume, and decays with its chain in the same event:
###   floor: U-238, Th-232, K-40 or U-235 in a region of the floor (rmVolume Floor), rmThreshold 1e60 (years): every
###          member of the chain decays, as in secular equilibrium (see macro/beam_steel_decay.mac);
###   radon: Rn-222 in the air inside the lead castle (rmVolume WorldPhys: the points in the world's own air, none in a
###          plate, bar, frame or the panel), rmThreshold 1 (year): the short-lived daughters decay, Pb-210 (22 y) and
###          below do not, as in room air.
### Only events with energy in the panel are written (/EventFilter 7); the number of decays is the run tree's n_events.
### The job macro sets the aliases bmSeed, bmEvents, bmDir, bmFile, bmPanel, bmPanelZ, bmIonZ, bmIonA, rmRegion, rmX,
### rmY, rmZ, rmHalfX, rmHalfY, rmHalfZ, rmVolume and rmThreshold, the target's /tof/target/composition and density, then
### executes this. Needs TOFmeter --preinit macro/preinit_lyso.mac (radioactive decay and fluorescence).
/tof/det/worldSize 420 420 300 cm
/tof/det/stack false
/tof/target/size 20 20 1 cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 33.0 cm
/control/execute macro/panel_{bmPanel}.mac
/tof/czt/position 0 0 {bmPanelZ} cm
/tof/blocks/add Floor G4_CONCRETE 0 0 -15 420 420 30 cm
/update
/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 7
/OutputDirectory {bmDir}
/OutputFile {bmFile}
/gun/seed {bmSeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 1
/gps/particle ion
/gps/ion {bmIonZ} {bmIonA} 0 0
/gps/pos/type Volume
/gps/pos/shape Para
/gps/pos/centre {rmX} {rmY} {rmZ} cm
/gps/pos/halfx {rmHalfX} cm
/gps/pos/halfy {rmHalfY} cm
/gps/pos/halfz {rmHalfZ} cm
/gps/pos/confine {rmVolume}
/gps/ang/type iso
/gps/ene/type Mono
/gps/ene/mono 0 keV
/process/had/rdm/thresholdForVeryLongDecayTime {rmThreshold} year
# Auger electrons off (their few keV stay where they are made), as in the beam jobs; fluorescence stays on
/process/em/auger false
/process/em/augerCascade false
# verbose 1: the log ends with "Number of events processed : <bmEvents>", which the job script looks for
/run/verbose 1
/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn {bmEvents}
